@page "/components/treeview/selection"

<DocsPage>
    <DocsPageHeader Title="Tree View - Selection Modes" Component="@nameof(VekTreeView<T>)">
        <Description>Configure single selection, toggle selection, or tri-state hierarchical checkbox selection across the tree.</Description>
    </DocsPageHeader>
    <DocsPageContent>

        <DocsPageSection>
            <SectionHeader Title="Hierarchical Checkbox Selection">
                <Description>
                    Set <CodeInline>SelectionMode</CodeInline> to <CodeInline>SelectionMode.MultiSelection</CodeInline> to show a checkbox for every selectable node. Selecting a parent checks its descendants, and <CodeInline>@@bind-SelectedValues</CodeInline> keeps the selected values in sync.
                    With <CodeInline>TriState</CodeInline> enabled, a parent shows an indeterminate checkbox while its descendants have a mixed selection. <CodeInline>AutoSelectParent</CodeInline> adds a parent value only after all selectable descendants are checked.
                    The example binds the same values to chips and lets you toggle read-only mode, indeterminate display, and parent synchronization.
                </Description>
            </SectionHeader>
            <SectionContent Code="@nameof(TreeViewMultiSelectionExample)" ShowCode="false">
                <TreeViewMultiSelectionExample />
            </SectionContent>
        </DocsPageSection>

        <DocsPageSection>
            <SectionHeader Title="Binding Items Directly">
                <Description>
                    <p>
                        You can directly bind the <CodeInline>Selected</CodeInline> and <CodeInline>Expanded</CodeInline> parameters on individual <CodeInline>VekTreeViewItem</CodeInline> components.
                    </p>
                    <br/>
                    <p>
                        While managing selection is typically done on the parent <CodeInline>VekTreeView</CodeInline> via <CodeInline>@@bind-SelectedValue</CodeInline> or <CodeInline>@@bind-SelectedValues</CodeInline>, direct item binding is particularly useful when creating custom interactions within an item template.
                    </p>
                </Description>
            </SectionHeader>
            <SectionContent Code="@nameof(TreeViewBindItemsExample)" ShowCode="false">
                <TreeViewBindItemsExample />
            </SectionContent>
        </DocsPageSection>

    </DocsPageContent>
</DocsPage>
